, {"key": "e_1_2_1_30_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF01244663"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_31_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S1054-3589(08)61160-6"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_32_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S0140-6736(63)90271-X"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_33_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/0006-2952(65)90102-4"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_34_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1111/j.1471-4159.1975.tb07626.x"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_35_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00421072"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_36_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/2251259b0"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_37_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00422612"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_38_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1001/archpsyc.1973.01750360053007"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_39_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00421379"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_40_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S0140-6736(75)92052-8"}, {"key": "e_1_2_1_41_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/236225b0"}], "container-title": ["Novartis Foundation Symposia", "Ciba Foundation Symposium 39 \u2010 Monoamine Oxidase and its Inhibition"], "link": [{"URL": "https://api.wiley.com/onlinelibrary/tdm/v1/articles/10.1002%2F9780470720219.ch12", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1002/9780470720219.ch12", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2023, 8, 25]], "date-time": "2023-08-25T08:29:37Z", "timestamp": 1692952177000}, "score": 21.752724, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/9780470720219.ch12"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[1976, 1]]}, "ISBN": ["9780470663318", "9780470720219"], "references-count": 40, "alternative-id": ["10.1002/9780470720219.ch12", "10.1002/SERIES1767", "10.1002/9780470720219"], "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1002/9780470720219.ch12", "archive": ["Portico"], "ISSN": ["1935-4657"], "issn-type": [{"value": "1935-4657", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[1976, 1]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 5]], "date-time": "2026-08-05T12:47:41Z", "timestamp": 1785934061417, "version": "3.56.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 1]], "date-time": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1767225600000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://www.uspto.gov/ip-policy/copyright-policy/copyright-basics"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Alignment research for large language models has focused primarily on model-centric interventions-fine-tuning, preference optimization, and decoding-time filters. These methods improve average behavior, yet they do not continuously observe or constrain the runtime trajectory of an agent as it acts in a tool-using environment. We present an observationcentered runtime safety architecture that treats semantic state as a measurable trajectory and separates safety into five strictly layered concerns: Observation, Geometry, Risk, Control, and (future) Execution. The architecture is realized as the SensOS Runtime Safety Layer through a staged experimental program. Heterogeneous agent events are normalized into an Observation Object and projected to a trajectory; a model-agnostic geometry engine estimates curvature, boundary distance, density, stability, and basin membership; a risk engine converts those descriptors into a continuous risk valuation with hysteresis and early warning; and a control engine maps risk to a graduated L0-L7 decision under an approval interlock. Execution against a live agent is intentionally excluded: control outputs are decisions only, pending a separate safety review. On a real Claude Code session (n = 489 events), end-to-end observation pipeline latency was 0.094 ms mean per event (alert-only; zero alerts at threshold 0.5). Geometry, risk, and control packages exhibit production-grade software engineering quality-full statement and branch test coverage (95/151/107 tests)-with measured sub-millisecond risk and control latencies (0.0067/0.0039 ms mean). These figures characterize software quality and microbenchmarks, not validated operational safety. We do not claim live intervention efficacy; we claim a coherent, measured, and architecturally honest decision spine for runtime safety without modifying foundation models.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.7177038", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 5]], "date-time": "2026-08-05T12:15:42Z", "timestamp": 1785932142000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Observation-Centered Runtime Safety for Foundation-Model Agents:&amp;nbsp;A Model-Agnostic Geometry\u2013Risk\u2013Control Architecture"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2688-8617", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Tomohiko", "family": "Nakamura", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 5]], "date-time": "2026-08-05T12:15:42Z", "timestamp": 1785932142000}, "score": 21.737446, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=7177038"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.7177038", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 1]], "date-time": "2026-08-01T14:52:58Z", "timestamp": 1785595978302, "version": "3.56.0"}, "reference-count": 32, "publisher": "Institution of Engineering and Technology (IET)", "issue": "6", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2016, 2, 19]], "date-time": "2016-02-19T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1455840000000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/termsAndConditions#vor"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["IET Computer Vision"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2016, 9]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Continuous action recognition in video is more complicated compared with traditional isolated action recognition. Besides the high variability of postures and appearances of each action, the complex temporal dynamics of continuous action makes this problem challenging. In this study, the authors propose a hierarchical framework combining convolutional neural network (CNN) and hidden Markov model (HMM), which recognises and segments continuous actions simultaneously. The authors utilise the CNN's powerful capacity of learning high level features directly from raw data, and use it to extract effective and robust action features. The HMM is used to model the statistical dependences over adjacent sub\u2010actions and infer the action sequences. In order to combine the advantages of these two models, the hybrid architecture of CNN\u2010HMM is built. The Gaussian mixture model is replaced by CNN to model the emission distribution of HMM. The CNN\u2010HMM model is trained using embedded Viterbi algorithm, and the data used to train CNN are labelled by forced alignment. The authors test their method on two public action dataset Weizmann and KTH. Experimental results show that the authors\u2019 method achieves improved recognition and segmentation accuracy compared with several other methods. The superior property of features learnt by CNN is also illustrated.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1049/iet-cvi.2015.0408", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2016, 2, 19]], "date-time": "2016-02-19T07:58:53Z", "timestamp": 1455868733000}, "page": "537-544", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 38, "title": ["Continuous action segmentation and recognition using hybrid convolutional neural network\u2010hidden Markov model model"], "prefix": "10.1049", "volume": "10", "author": [{"given": "Jun", "family": "Lei", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "College of Information Systems and Management National University of Defense Technology Changsha People's Republic of China"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Guohui", "family": "Li", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "College of Information Systems and Management National University of Defense Technology Changsha People's Republic of China"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Jun", "family": "Zhang", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "College of Information Systems and Management National University of Defense Technology Changsha People's Republic of China"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Qiang", "family": "Guo", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "College of Information Systems and Management National University of Defense Technology Changsha People's Republic of China"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Dan", "family": "Tu", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "College of Information Systems and Management National University of Defense Technology Changsha People's Republic of China"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "265", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2016, 2, 19]]}, "reference": [{"key": "e_1_2_8_2_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1109/34.910878"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_3_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1109/CVPR.2008.4587721"}, {"issue": "12", "key": "e_1_2_8_4_2", "first-page": "1395", "article-title": "Actions as space\u2010time shapes", "volume": "29", "author": "Blank M.", "year": "2007", "journal-title": "IEEE Tr